    "chunk_size_bytes": 764,
    "chunk_text": "Senthilverl Holdings increases stake in C M Holdings above 10%\n\nSenthilverl Holdings Ltd. has increased its shareholding in C M Holdings PLC to over 10% of the company\u2019s issued capital following a transaction on 30 October 2025.\n\nSenthilverl Holdings bought one million shares at Rs. 71 each for Rs. 71 million, raising its total holding to 15,488,966 shares or 10.19% of C M Holdings\u2019 issued capital of 152 million shares. Senthilverl Holdings is the second largest shareholder of C M Holdings.\n\nC M Holdings closed Friday at Rs. 70.90 a share down by 10 cents.\n\nAs of end-September 2025, the company reported a net asset value per share of Rs. 467, up from Rs. 246 a year ago. The Colombo Fort Land and Building PLC is the top shareholder with a 63.5% stake."
  },
