    "md5": "7ec2a0630060ada80ab77120c80c4b37",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2011,
    "chunk_text": "New national operations unit to shield Sri Lanka\u2019s forests to be unveiled today\n\nSri Lanka will today unveil a major national initiative aimed at strengthening environmental protection, with the launch of the \u201cWana Surakuma\u201d Integrated Operations Unit, a unified mechanism established to shield the country\u2019s forests, wildlife and ecological heritage.\n\nThe initiative, introduced under the guidance of the President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, and led by Environment Minister Dr. Damika Patabendige, forms a central part of the government\u2019s thrust toward building an environmentally responsible nation under the theme \u201cA Sustainable Biosphere, An Evergreen Life.\u201d\n\nThe unit will be officially launched today at the Wildlife and Forest Conservation Wing of the Environment Ministry premises,\u00a0 Hector Kobbekaduwa Mawatha, Colombo 07. State Minister Anton Jayakody will join the proceedings.\n\n\u201cWana Surakuma\u201d brings together officers from the Forest Department, Department of Wildlife Conservation, the Police Special Task Force (STF) and the Tri-forces, enabling rapid and coordinated intervention against environmental crimes.\n\nThe public will be able to report illegal logging, forest fires, encroachments, wildlife crime and other threats through the 24/7 emergency hotline 1995, designed to ensure immediate action and reliable information flow.\n\nA central operations hub will collect, classify and analyse data on forest and wildlife-related offences. The unit will employ drones, satellite imagery, GPS-based surveillance and real-time field communication to identify high-risk areas and monitor forest cover.\n\nDr. Ravindra Kariyawasam, Senior Advisor to the Ministry of Environment, highlighted the significance of the launch:\n\n\u201cFor the first time, Sri Lanka is building a single, technologically empowered platform to detect, analyse and respond to environmental crimes in real time. This is not merely enforcement, it is a national shield for our forests, wildlife and biodiversity.\u201d"
  },
