    "md5": "b3fc026d6fbdc5452a02d709e66b4dae",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1628,
    "chunk_text": "Unforgettable 31st night in Colombo!\n\n\u2018Dancing Through the Decades,\u2019 at Cinnamon Life, is shaping up to be an unforgettable 31st night in Colombo!\n\nIn fact, the response to this gigantic New Year\u2019s Eve event has been overwhelming, and Sohan is convinced that Cinnamon Life is heading for a sell out in early December.\n\nIt is all happening on 31st December, 2025, from 8:00 PM onwards, at the Lumina Ballroom, Cinnamon Life.\n\n31st night revellers will have for company Sri Lanka\u2019s top artistes, including Sohan Weerasinghe, Corrine Almeida, Geoffrey Fernando, Clifford Richard, Rukshan Perera, Damian Wickramatillake, and Falan Andrea, and dance enthusiasts can groove to the hits from the \u201980s, \u201990s, and 2000s, with two bands, Flame and AROH, driving the party forward.\n\nThe night, according to Sohan, will culminate in a dazzling countdown to welcome 2026, with a sumptuous gourmet buffet and traditional Sri Lankan breakfast to follow.\n\nSohan also mentioned that many expats are coming from Sydney, Melbourne and Perth, and also London and LA, for \u2018Dancing Through the Decades.\u2019\n\nWith an incredible lineup of artistes and a night full of music, dance, and celebration, it\u2019s most certainly going to be a fantastic way to bid farewell to 2025 and welcome 2026 \u2026 at Cinnamon Life.\n\nSri Lanka hosts IFALPA \u201cPositive Safety Culture\u201d workshop, strengthening regional and international aviation safety collaboration\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
