    "chunk_text": "Carrots for hair growth\n\nLots of us tend to have problems with our hair \u2026 wondering how to have a good hair growth.\n\nThis week I\u2019ve worked out a few remedies for you to try out \u2013 carrot hair masks.\n\nYou will need 01 carrot, 02 tablespoons of olive oil, 01 onion, and 02 tablespoons of lemon juice.\n\nCut the onion and carrot into tiny pieces, and process them in a food processor. Add the lemon juice and olive oil to this paste and then apply it to your hair and leave it for 15 minutes.\n\nYou will need 02 carrots, \u00bd avocado, and 02 tablespoons of honey.\n\nCut the two carrots into small pieces and, together with the half avocado, blend them into a paste. Add the honey and stir until a smooth consistency is reached.\n\nApply this paste to your scalp, and hair, rubbing it in for 30 minutes, and then wash it off with a gentle shampoo.\n\nCut the carrot into small chunks and mix it in a food processor. Then add the coconut oil and make a thick paste.\n\nGive your scalp and hair a thorough application of this mask, let it sit for 20 minutes, and then use a mild shampoo to wash it off.\n\nYou will need 02 carrots, 04-05 pieces of ripe papaya, and 02 tablespoons of yoghurt.\n\nCut the carrots into small pieces and, in a food processor, blend the carrot pieces with the papaya and yoghurt until you obtain a smooth paste.\n\nApply the mask to your scalp and hair and let it sit for 30 minutes, and then wash it off, using a gentle shampoo.\n\nYou will need 01 carrot, 02 tablespoons yoghurt, and 01 banana.\n\nCut the carrots and bananas into tiny pieces and blend them, in a food processor, with the yoghurt.\n\nCover your entire head with this mask, then cover it with a shower cap, and let it sit for 30 minutes. Use a gentle shampoo to wash it off.\n\nAwakening a Generation: Mentoring Sri Lanka\u2019s Youth for Purpose and Progress\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment