    "md5": "e79238dda2d9a990d01ac08531f3a3f3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1920,
    "chunk_text": "A recent CNN report from Nepal highlights how Generation Z, long described as \u201cdigital natives,\u201d is now transforming that online fluency into political force. Frustrated by corruption and emboldened by connectivity, young protesters organised through Instagram, Discord, and other networks\u2014even under state attempts to silence them with internet shutdowns. Their mass mobilisation led to violent clashes,\u00a0resulting in many deaths and destruction.\n\nIn reflecting on Nepal\u2019s Gen Z uprising, Sri Lankan youth\u2014beyond just Gen Z\u2014must also turn inward and ask a deeper question: Do we truly understand our own national identity? Amid the digital noise and global influences, there is a growing disconnect from Sri Lanka\u2019s cultural roots, values, and ethical foundations. This is precisely why Sri Lanka must look inward and revive movements grounded in national purpose\u2014much like those once led by Ven. Madihe Pannasiha Mahanayake Thera. He founded the Dharma Vijaya Foundation with the vision of transforming Sri Lanka into a Dhamma D\u012bpa\u2014a nation guided by compassion, wisdom, and moral discipline. At a time of growing youth disillusionment, his Thurunu Saviya movement offered a lifeline: a platform for youth rehabilitation, leadership, and moral development, particularly in response to rising drug abuse and social unrest. His fearless advocacy helped shape national policy\u2014from making Poya days public holidays to protecting Buddhist schools and heritage, reinforcing the role of cultural identity in nation-building. Ven. Madihe Pannasiha\u2019s legacy reminds us that real transformation demands more than slogans or social media campaigns\u2014it requires rooted leadership, moral courage, and a collective return to values that define us. As Sri Lanka\u2019s youth navigate the noise of global trends and digital distractions, this blend of tradition and action is not just relevant\u2014it\u2019s essential."
