    "md5": "e91dad7e7b615d2cfc8ede20ba93bbaa",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1651,
    "chunk_text": "Bosch celebrates 10 years in Sri Lanka\n\nGroup officials, guests and invitees at the Make a Toast Gala of Bosch's 10th anniversary celebration\n\nMarking a decade of innovation and partnership between Germany and Sri Lanka, Bosch recently celebrated 10 years of operations in the country, reflecting on its impact, technological excellence, and commitment to sustainability progress.\n\nBosch, a leading global supplier of technology and services, celebrated its journey in Sri Lanka with an event themed \u2018Transforming a Decade. Inspiring the Future\u2019. The grand anniversary celebration was attended by Science and Technology Minister Prof. Chrishantha Abeysena, Bosch\u2019s regional leadership, Government representatives, business partners, and academia.\n\nSpeaking at the event, the Minister highlighted that Bosch\u2019s contribution went beyond advanced technologies and helped cultivate an ecosystem that strengthens industries, develops skills, and aligns Sri Lanka with global standards.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka\u2019s vision is to build a modern technological economy, one that tries on research, innovation and digital fascination. To achieve that, we need not only policies and infrastructure, but also trusted partners who believe in our potential and invest in our people,\u201d he said.\n\nHe noted that partnerships like Bosch\u2019s demonstrated how international investment could accelerate national development by transferring knowledge, building ecosystems, and inspiring new generations of innovators. The Minister called for continued focus on research, development, and local innovation to ensure Sri Lanka evolved from a consumer to a creator of technology."
  },
