    "chunk_size_bytes": 1962,
    "chunk_text": "Around the time I went to Colombo, the intense American influence through organisations like YFC was clear and deleterious. A typical evangelical meeting would have youths led by an older person directing and culminating it with an \u201cAre you Born Again?\u201d sermon.\n\nThese games attracted attendance. By the late 1980s YFC had a full-time worker in Jaffna with meetings in Chundikuli and Uduvil. Locals were scandalised when now westernised youthful boys and girls were engaged together in the contact sport of volleyball in the Uduvil playground as warmup for the meeting.\n\nThese organisations claimed not to be churches and not in competition with churches. However, they had their meetings on Sunday evenings, and attendees would cut Church in the mornings saying they had a worship service in the evening. Priests were upset.\n\nYFC\u2019s immense success in terms of attendance came from making the youth feel Western, if not American, and giving them access to members of the opposite sex whom they normally cannot speak to.\n\nWith increasing Western influence, today, 50 years later, things are worse. Those days\u2019 youth in development are now pastors and usually of depressed backgrounds as the upper castes with money and English have fled. Some new leaders forcibly kiss students and when the abused student dares to file a complaint, the other leaders suppress the complaint, claiming to safeguard institutional reputation. (I have separate affidavits from two girl students in Trincomalee on which I have no Board support for any punishment against the offending Baldaeus Theological College board members).\n\nAlready we see these aspiring pastors getting scholarships to read for degrees in India, England, Scotland, Canada and Amerca. Based on \u201cexperience,\u201d they get MA degrees without a BA. Set up thereafter as qualified pastors and exploiting their foreign connections, they attract foreign funds which they then steal and build personal mansions."
