    "chunk_text": "Already we see these aspiring pastors getting scholarships to read for degrees in India, England, Scotland, Canada and Amerca. Based on \u201cexperience,\u201d they get MA degrees without a BA. Set up thereafter as qualified pastors and exploiting their foreign connections, they attract foreign funds which they then steal and build personal mansions.\n\nIt is these magic words that have attracted many criminals and child and women molesters to become Christian clergy. God loves and forgives is an excuse for every sin, with no room for repentence and absolution.\n\nI too wonder how these organisations talk up the Grahams when I have heard them boasting of the Grahams in my university days. Recently my late brother was Dean at Colombo Theological Seminary (CTS) and I was a Lecturer teaching Anglican Heritage there. He was asked by the CTS Board to assign teaching to a Minister (as I recall at the Four Square Gospel Church) who was habitually chased off from parish to parish for abusing women and had run out of places to be posted to where his antecedents were unknown.\n\nHis big brother was the head of his Church and on the CTS Board.\u00a0 My brother refused because that would endanger his students. But the CTS Board chair, a Youth for Christ and Graham man, ordered my brother to take on this man known for pawing women. It was a reason why my brother left CTS and started Baldaeus Theological Seminary in Trincomalee\n\nI join the BBC in asking, \u201cWhat makes so many see this man [Trump], who isn\u2019t known to have an especially strong faith, as sent from God? And what does that say about Christianity more broadly in a country where the numbers of churchgoers are in rapid decline?\u201d\n\nSri Lankan Christianity is in real danger as these Anglo-Christians take over the new free churches where their dispossessed caste membership is looking for ways to enrich themselves, marry stylish brides and climb up the social ladder because they are more likely accepted overlooking caste because they are baptised."
