    "md5": "74042baf7b5a0bd7c87f132d8825f3d1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1891,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan Christianity is in real danger as these Anglo-Christians take over the new free churches where their dispossessed caste membership is looking for ways to enrich themselves, marry stylish brides and climb up the social ladder because they are more likely accepted overlooking caste because they are baptised.\n\nIn the new Christianity defined by the anointed Gold-Bible selling Trump, free-sex is the norm. We can see how that has already infected Sri Lankan Evangelicals. In their view, remarriage with surving spouse is monogamy so long as there is divorce. The Muslims\u2019 and the Mormons\u2019 polygamy are vast improvements because the wife is not thrown out and has to be provided for. I have seen in these dispossessed-caste churches, divorce being encouraged on flimsy pretexts to a get the man for one of their own women. Not a small number of clergymen are divorced and remarried or engaged in adultery.\n\nTrump himself has been accused by his first wife wife Ivana in a divorce deposition of\u00a0raping her in a fit of rage in 1989. For a partial list of Trump\u2019s accusers, see here.\n\nIvana married twice more after Trump (and twice before him) with Trump hosting the $3 million reception or giving her a $3 million ring. It shows how polygamy for Trump and polyandry for Ivana are within Christian monogamy because they divorced.\n\nThe Bible is replete with the idea that we should choose our company carefully. The Book of Psalms in its opening verse advises us. \u201cBlessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked, nor stand in the way of sinners, nor sit in the seat of the scornful.\u201d Proverbs 13:20 uses the word wicked for scornful, while St. Paul (1 Corintians, 15:33) admonishes us \u201cBad company ruins good morals.\u201d\n\nChoosing good company is advice\u00a0 that we (whether Christian, Muslim, Hindu or Buddhist) received as children and give our children."
