    "chunk_text": "The Bible is replete with the idea that we should choose our company carefully. The Book of Psalms in its opening verse advises us. \u201cBlessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked, nor stand in the way of sinners, nor sit in the seat of the scornful.\u201d Proverbs 13:20 uses the word wicked for scornful, while St. Paul (1 Corintians, 15:33) admonishes us \u201cBad company ruins good morals.\u201d\n\nChoosing good company is advice\u00a0 that we (whether Christian, Muslim, Hindu or Buddhist) received as children and give our children.\n\nAt an Election Commission dinner I was reserved a seat at the high table next to General Shavendra Silva. I had little choice but to smile and shake hands \u2013 although the US has imposed sanctions on him in the form of a travel ban on him and his family entering the United States. He was found accountable through command responsibility for \u201cgross violations of human rights, namely extrajudicial killings, by the 58th division under his command\u201d when up to 70,000 Tamil civilians were killed.\n\nThis brings me to President Donald Trump and his sex crazed disrespect for women. Good Christians cannot hobnob with him or seek jobs in his administration. But to climb in their career, many do.\n\nIn a recording brought out by The Washington Post and broadcast by\u00a0 ABC News, the conversation goes like this in a 2005 recording that became public in October 2016. Donald Trump in an off-camera conversation with then Access Hollywood host Billy Bush boasts of kissing and groping women without consent:\n\n\u201cYou know, I\u2019m automatically attracted to beautiful\u2026 I just start kissing them. It\u2019s like a magnet. Just kiss. I don\u2019t even wait.\u201d \u2026\u201dAnd when you\u2019re a star they let you do it\u2026 You can do anything\u201d. \u2026 \u201cGrab them by the pussy\u201d. \u2026\u201dYou can do anything\u201d.\n\nIn the same recording, Trump discussed an unsuccessful attempt to seduce a married woman:\n\n\u201cI moved on her, and I failed. I\u2019ll admit it. I did try and f**k her. She was married\u201d."
