    "chunk_size_bytes": 1774,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo Academy of Hospitality Management celebrates Australian qualification achievements at 13th graduation ceremony\n\nThe Colombo Academy of Hospitality Management, Sri Lanka\u2019s largest private hospitality, food, tourism, and events education provider, conducted its 13th Graduation Ceremony in partnership with the William Angliss Institute (RTO: 3045) in style at the prestigious Shangri-La Hotel, Colombo.\n\nThe graduation ceremony commenced with a traditional Kandyan dance performance that impressed the audience, including the William Angliss Institute delegation, followed by a welcome address by Grant Dreher, Chief Executive Officer, William Angliss Institute, Australia.\n\nThe Chief Guest, Diarra Wickremasinghe \u2013 Director, Owner, and Founder of Pink Salt Restaurant, Brown Sugar Caf\u00e9, Isle Amore Pizzeria, Brown Sugar Doughnuts, and Daily Dough, and an alumna of the Institute, delivered a motivating speech about her success in the hospitality industry and her future aspirations, which was inspiring for all present.\n\nThe globally recognised Australian qualifications awarded by the William Angliss Institute included the Certificate IV in Kitchen Management, Certificate IV in Patisserie, Diploma of Event Management, Advanced Diploma of Travel and Tourism Management, and the Advanced Diploma of Hospitality Management.\n\nThe celebrations continued with the announcement of numerous special awards for individual students\u2019 achievements. Over 600 students, parents, and industry representatives attended this dazzling event to witness a significant milestone for the graduates as they celebrated their academic journey and future in the hospitality industry. A delightful lunch was catered to all attendees after the conclusion of the graduation ceremony."
