    "chunk_text": "Bourse upbeat over positive effects of Budget 2026; investor sentiment up\n\nThe CSE was upbeat over the 2026 budget yesterday, with the consequence that both indices moved upwards amid positive investor sentiments.The All Share Price Index went up by 225.7 points, while the S and P SL20 rose by 44.51 points. Turnover stood at Rs 6.7 billion with 11 crossings.\n\nThe top seven crossings were: DFCC 1.5 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 256 million; its shares traded at Rs 154.75, Laugfs Gas 2.8 million shares crossed for Rs 199 million, its shares traded at Rs 73, People\u2019s Leasing and Finance five million shares crossed for Rs 145 million; its shares sold at Rs 29, JKH 4.5 million shares crossed for Rs 97.6 million; its shares sold at Rs 21.80, Sunshine Holdings one million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 39 million; its shares traded at Rs 39, Watawela Plantations 500,000 shares crossed for Rs 27 million; its shares traded at Rs 53.50 and Sierra Cables 800,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 25.6 million; its shares traded at Rs 32.\n\nIn the retail market top seven companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; Laugfs Gas Rs 446 million (6.2 million shares traded), Sampath Bank Rs 301 million (two million shares traded), Bogala Graphite Rs 290 million (2.2 million shares traded), Sunshine Holdings Rs 242 million (6.2 million shares traded), JKH Rs 240 million (10.9 million shares traded), Colombo Dockyard Rs 219 million (480000 shares traded) and Kotagala Plantations Rs 205 million (18 million shares traded). During the day 209 million share volumes changed hands in 44670 transactions.\n\nIt is said that mixed reactions were noted in most of sectors. The banking and finance sector performed well; especially DFCC, while the mining and plantations sectors too performed well; especially, Bogala Graphite and Kotagala Plantations."
