    "md5": "e8f76ea8d3c6fc53f08e94c73c351135",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1915,
    "chunk_text": "A knotty legal issue\n\nThe JVP-led NPP government has apparently taken a leaf out of its immediate predecessor\u2019s book, where election postponements are concerned. It has said the much-delayed Provincial Council (PC) elections will be held only after the completion of the delimitation process, which is a prerequisite for the implementation of the mixed proportional system.\n\nThe Election Commission (EC) is reported to have said the completion of the delimitation process will take about one year. The NPP is losing cooperative society elections, which are considered political windsocks, and therefore the government will try every trick in the book to delay the PC polls as long as possible.\n\nThe postponement of PC elections was widely considered a political issue, and it was thought that the most effective way to sort it out was to crank up pressure on the government, but former EC Chairman Mahinda Deshapriya has shed light on a legal dimension of the problem.\n\nHe has said the Governors are keeping the PCs under their control in violation of a Supreme Court ruling that the PCs be governed by elected councillors. He revealed this at a conference held on Wednesday. He is au fait with election laws and judicial decisions pertaining to them. Those who are genuinely desirous of having the PC polls held without further delay can now explore the possibility of seeking a judicial intervention.\n\nDuring the previous government, the JVP-led NPP raked the then President Ranil Wickremesinghe over the coals for postponing the Local Government polls in defiance of an SC order. It joined the other Opposition parties in demanding that the SLPP-UNP government comply with the SC order that funds be allocated for the mini polls. Going by the former EC Chief\u2019s contention, the incumbent NPP government and its leaders have done something similar; they have been keeping the PCs under the Governors illegally."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-08-islandlk-46520e44",
    "num": "islandlk-46520e44",
    "date_str": "2025-11-08",
    "description": "A knotty legal issue",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/a-knotty-legal-issue/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "islandlk",
