    "chunk_size_bytes": 1372,
    "chunk_text": "A message of hope on the move: Kangaroo Cabs drives breast cancer awareness\n\nIn a unique awareness campaign this October, a simple taxi ride became a vehicle for a life-saving message. Kangaroo Cabs, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading transport providers, turned its entire fleet into moving reminders for Breast Cancer Awareness Month by adorning its headrests with distinctive pink ribbons.\n\nEach ribbon was paired with a QR code, allowing passengers on thousands of daily journeys from airport pickups to intercity travel to instantly access vital information about the importance of early detection directly on their phones.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re proud that a simple taxi ride could carry a message that matters. A pink ribbon has gone a long way,\u201d a spokesperson for Kangaroo Cabs said, noting the positive feedback received from passengers and drivers alike.\n\nThe company stated that by merging the daily commute with a critical cause, they demonstrated how awareness can travel seamlessly into the community, reinforcing that early detection is the most effective defence against breast cancer.\n\nCanon & Metropolitan celebrate \u2018leadership\u2019 in Sri Lanka\u2019s printer hardware industry\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
