    "md5": "7772ede71211ed687839682a0a35d706",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1795,
    "chunk_text": "Apart from the similarity of venue, the Nugegoda rallies of Mahinda Sulanga and Mahaa Jana Handa are  totally different. The JVP/NPP govt seems to be in a dominant position vis a vis the opposition. President AKD is currently the single most popular mass figure in Sri Lankan politics. There is no one of equal stature among opposition leaders.\n\nThe issues likely to be raised by the opposition parties are of little consequence at present to the public. Furthermore there are many who feel that the opposition  politicians are panicking due to the fear of being penalised through the anti-corruption campaign conducted by the Govt.\n\nMoreover despite some internal tension, there is overall unity within Govt ranks. As such there is very little chance of the opposition promoting dissension within the Government at the present time. In contrast there is  much disparity among and within the opposition.  There is a lot of suspicion that Namal Rajapaksa and the SLPP are attempting to hijack the rally as a promotional stunt for  Namal\u2019s 2029 presidential candidacy.\n\nThe chief opposition party led by the accredited leader of the opposition keeps aloof from the protest campaign. It is like the Ramayana being staged without Lord Rama.Moreover President Dissanayake complimented Opposition Leader Premadasa in Parliament  for keeping away from Nugegoda. It appears that in typical fashion,Sajith is insecure about Ranil Wickremesinghe and Namal Rajapakse.\n\nAgainst this backdrop  the prospects of the Nugegoda rally being a joint opposition sucees that could lay the foundation for greater opposition unity seems a remote possibility.Furthermore the fragile semblance of unity among opposition parties  currently visible is likely to shatter if and when provincial council elections are held."
  },
