    "chunk_size_bytes": 1461,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Saudi Arabia pledge to deepen political and economic ties\n\nForeign Affairs and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath (left) meets Saudi Arabian Foreign Affairs Minister Prince Faisal bin Farhan Al Saud\n\nForeign Affairs and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath met with Saudi Arabia\u2019s Minister of Foreign Affairs, Prince Faisal bin Farhan Al Saud, in Riyadh during his visit to attend the 26th UN World Tourism Organisation (UNWTO) General Assembly.\n\nIn a post on X, Herath said the meeting focused on strengthening bilateral political and economic cooperation between the two countries. He briefed the Saudi side on Sri Lanka\u2019s investment-friendly climate and invited Saudi investors to explore opportunities emerging across key sectors of the Sri Lankan economy.\n\nHerath also announced that the first-ever Sri Lanka\u2013Saudi Arabia Business Council will be established between the Federations of Chambers of both countries during his visit. The new body is expected to enhance private sector engagement and serve as a platform to promote trade and investment.\n\nThe Foreign Minister commended Saudi Arabia\u2019s leadership in seeking a lasting solution to the Palestine issue and reaffirmed Sri Lanka\u2019s longstanding support for the Palestinian cause.\n\nDuring the meeting, Prince Faisal officially presented commemorative stamps issued by Saudi Post to mark the 50th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Sri Lanka and Saudi Arabia."
