    "time_ut": 1762728480.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-11-10-dailyftlk-bafa031f-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5e38a966e601b1f08df0c50bd1403ac2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1673,
    "chunk_text": "Hong Kong\u2019s SiS Group takes up  controlling stake in Gestetner of Ceylon\n\nFrom left: SiS Directors Lim Hwee Noi and Lim Hwee Hai, SiS Chairman and Gestetner of Ceylon incoming Chairman Lim Kiah Meng, Gestetner of Ceylon outgoing Chairman Sayed Jamaldeen Anzsar, and Director A.R. Rasiah\n\nSiS International Holdings Ltd., (SiS) recently invested in a controlling 50.01% stake in Gestetner of Ceylon PLC (Gestetner), a leading player in the office automation sector in Sri Lanka, through World Elite Ltd., one of its Hong Kong-based subsidiaries for Rs. 318.655 million.\n\nSiS Chairman and incoming Chairman of Gestetner Lim Kiah Meng said: \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s resilient and growing economy, along with increasing demand for office automation and IT services, presents a strategic opportunity for us to strengthen our regional footprint. Gestetner\u2019s strong market position, established brand equity, and proven operational integrity align perfectly with SiS\u2019 values and vision. By combining our regional expertise with Gestetner\u2019s local market knowledge, we aim to deliver innovative solutions and create sustainable value for businesses in Sri Lanka so as to enhance shareholder value for both SiS and Gestetner.\u201d\n\nFounded in Singapore in 1983 and started as a distributor of IT products, SiS International Holdings Limited has been listed on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange since 1992. Today, it has grown to become a dynamic leading distribution company with the largest network across five countries in Asia Pacific. Over the years, it has also successfully expanded into investments in technology and securities, real estate investment, and asset management segments."
  },
