    "md5": "dfb5d678e12e3c15a4a2abb6e60e5a03",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1774,
    "chunk_text": "Hemas Consumer Brands sets national benchmark as \u201cOverall Winner\u201d at JASTECA Awards 2025\n\nHemas Consumer Brands (HCB) was honoured with the prestigious title of \u201cOverall Winner\u201d at the JASTECA Awards 2025. This recognition reaffirms HCB\u2019s position as a national benchmark in operational excellence (lean management), driven by its influential adoption of Japanese 5S and Kaizen practices.\n\nStanding out among a highly competitive field of multinational corporations and local enterprises of all scales, HCB was celebrated for its consistent delivery of best-in-class performance, rooted in a bottom-up performance culture.\n\nOrganised by the Japan Sri Lanka Technical and Cultural Association, the JASTECA Awards have been the pinnacle of operational excellence recognition in Sri Lanka since 1996. They honour organisations that embody Japanese principles of quality, productivity, employee engagement, and corporate social responsibility.\n\nAward winners are selected through a rigorous evaluation process, including both onsite and offsite audits conducted by Japanese and Sri Lankan experts. These assessments focus on each organisation\u2019s operational strength and the competitive edge it creates.\n\nHemas Consumer Brands Managing Director Sabrina Esufally said: \u201cBeing named the Overall Winner at JASTECA 2025, among the best organisations in Sri Lanka, is an immense honour\u2014especially as the awards return after a five-year hiatus. This recognition celebrates our operational excellence, achieved through our people\u2019s relentless pursuit of perfection and commitment to eliminating waste. It also reinforces our purpose of enriching lives through products that are not only of the highest quality but are made responsibly, sustainably, and efficiently.\u201d"
  },
