    "md5": "d50cdc7b4f62422f04c6b6a876adfb98",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1752,
    "chunk_text": "Sampath Bank honoured at the Presidential Environmental Awards 2025 for its commitment to a Greener Sri Lanka\n\nSampath Bank PLC was honoured at the 11th Annual Presidential Environmental Awards 2025, organised by the Central Environmental Authority (CEA), held recently at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH), Colombo. The ceremony took place under the distinguished patronage of Anura Kumara Dissanayake, President of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe Bank received the national recognition Silver Award in the category of Environmentally Friendly Private Institution, marking a defining milestone as its first-ever honour at the Presidential Environmental Awards. Presented annually by the Central Environmental Authority, the awards celebrate individuals and organisations that demonstrate exceptional commitment to environmental conservation and sustainable development. Through this recognition, Sampath Bank\u2019s continued efforts in integrating sustainability into its operations, promoting responsible banking, and supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s national sustainability goals were acknowledged at a national level.\n\nCommenting on this achievement, Sanjaya Gunawardena, Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer of Sampath Bank PLC stated, \u201cThis recognition is a reflection of our collective purpose to build a banking culture that respects people, resources, wildlife and the planet. As a Bank that places sustainability at the heart of its business model, we are deeply honoured to be recognised by the Central Environmental Authority and the Government of Sri Lanka. It inspires us to continue driving positive environmental change that benefits not only our customers but the nation at large.\u201d"
