    "chunk_text": "Budget 2026 continues to energize bourse, bolstered by positive corporate earnings\n\nThe CSE\u2019s bull-run continued yesterday as well driven by positive investor sentiment continuing to radiate from the 2026 Budget, good corporate quarterly earnings/results and better micro economic performance.\n\nThe All- Share Price Index went up by 79.56 points, while the S and P SL20 rose by 33.90 points. Turnover stood at Rs 8.2 billion with 19 crossings.\n\nTop seven crossings were; E B Creasy four million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 168 million and its shares traded at Rs 67, DFCC 1.3 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 214 million; its shares traded at Rs 159.50, LOLC Holdings 185,000 shares crossed for Rs 100 million; its shares sold at Rs 545, Commercial Bank 452,328 shares crossed for Rs 97.8 million; its shares traded at Rs 216.50, HNB (Non-Voting) 82000 shares crossed for Rs 93 million; its shares fetched Rs 330, Sampath Bank 470,000 shares crossed for Rs 73.5 million; its shares sold at Rs 155 and Distilleries one million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 55 million; its shares fetched Rs 55.\n\nIn the retail market top seven companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; RIL Properties Rs 392 million (10.6 million shares traded), DFCC Bank Rs 346 million (two million shares traded), Bogala Graphite Rs 342 million (two million shares traded), SLT Rs 331 million (3.9 million shares traded), Renuka Agri Rs 290 million (38 million shares traded), Access Engineering Rs 284.5 million (4.3 million shares traded) and Richard Pieris Rs 282.6 million (7.5 million shares traded). During the day 223 million shares volumes changed hands in 52000 transactions."
