    "md5": "2137f1235e600acd7346d4d2da129b0b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1778,
    "chunk_text": "30th Annual General Meeting of Sri Lanka\u2013Korea Business Council of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce\n\nFrom left (seated): SLKBC Adviser Priyantha Mendis, Embassy of the Republic of Korea to Sri Lanka Research officer Minwoo Jo, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Sri Lanka Miyon Lee, SLKBC President Shamil Mendis, SLKBC Senior Vice President Patali Karunarathne, SLKBC Immediate Past President Asitha Martis, The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce Yashodha Fernando; (standing): JGK Holdings Kaveeshi Weliwattha, SLKBC Honorary Member John Shiran Dissanayake; BOV Capital Prajeeth Balasubramaniam; SLKBC Honorary Member Mahen Kariyawasan, Abans Emudu Perera; A. Baur & Co. Devapriya Arthanayake\n\nThe Sri Lanka\u2013Korea Business Council (SLKBC) of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce held its 30th Annual General Meeting with Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Sri Lanka Miyon Lee gracing the event as Chief Guest.\n\nAmbassador Lee highlighted South Korea\u2019s robust economic outlook under President Lee Jae-myung\u2019s administration, which has embarked on a new five-year economic development plan. She noted that the successful hosting of the APEC Leaders\u2019 Meeting emphasised Korea\u2019s role in supporting global economic dialogue and easing geopolitical tensions.\n\nReflecting on the global economic environment, the Ambassador shared that despite lingering uncertainties, international growth forecasts continue to improve. She emphasised Korea\u2019s strong fundamentals\u2014low unemployment, stable inflation, and resilient consumer and business sentiment\u2014driving expected GDP growth recovery in 2026. Korea\u2019s leadership in advanced manufacturing sectors such as semiconductors, shipbuilding, defence, and cultural industries was underscored as key contributors to sustained growth."
  },
