    "chunk_text": "Reflecting on the global economic environment, the Ambassador shared that despite lingering uncertainties, international growth forecasts continue to improve. She emphasised Korea\u2019s strong fundamentals\u2014low unemployment, stable inflation, and resilient consumer and business sentiment\u2014driving expected GDP growth recovery in 2026. Korea\u2019s leadership in advanced manufacturing sectors such as semiconductors, shipbuilding, defence, and cultural industries was underscored as key contributors to sustained growth.\n\nSpear International Ltd., Shamil Mendis was elected President of the Council for 2025/2026. Mendis reaffirmed the Council\u2019s mission to advance trade, investment, tourism, and business collaboration between Sri Lanka and Korea.\n\nHe highlighted key initiatives undertaken during the year; including a session on \u201cKorea\u2019s current economy, business environment and opportunities for joint collaborations,\u201d a networking evening involving the members, government officials and representatives from the Embassy, and a collaborative event with the Council for start-ups on navigating the Korean market and opportunities for Sri Lankan businesses. The Council also hosted a highly acclaimed session on \u2018Sri Lanka\u2019s Future Forecast Scenarios and Challenges\u2019 featuring leading Sri Lankan Economists, as well as a discussion on \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s Export Prospect? Challenges. Opportunities. Reforms\u201d led by an industry expert to explore strategies for expanding Sri Lanka\u2019s global export footprint, particularly in sectors with untapped potential. Furthermore, a visit to Port City Colombo was arranged to explore investment avenues for Korean enterprises."
