    "md5": "393818ed04f3d898cfeffb1b9ff6cbf9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1919,
    "chunk_text": "CBL Foods International wins Global Performance Excellence Award \u2013 \u201cBest in Class\u201d\n\nCBL Foods International Head of Quality, Safety and Sustainability Tony Ukwattage collects award from APQO\u00a0officials at 30th APQO International Conference held in Beijing, China from 15 to 17 October\n\nCBL Foods International Ltd., a subsidiary of CBL Group, has been recognised with the Global Performance Excellence Award (GPEA) 2025 \u2013 Best in Class, presented by the Asia Pacific Quality Organisation (APQO) at its 30th International Conference held in Beijing, China.\n\nThe company was also honoured with the APQO International Best Practice \u2013 Silver Award at the same forum.\n\nCBL Foods International Ltd., Chief Executive Officer Kamal Geeganage said, \u201cQuality has always been our number one priority at CBL Group. It is the foundation of our reputation and trust. We never compromise on quality because every product that leaves our facilities carries the pride of our people and the promise of our purpose. As a company with humble Sri Lankan roots and a growing international footprint, we are proud to set benchmarks for the confectionery industry\u2014proving that a Sri Lankan business can achieve and sustain world-class standards.\u201d\n\nThe Global Performance Excellence Awards, organised by APQO, are the only formal international recognition for business excellence in the Asia-Pacific region. The awards promote the adoption of world-class quality and performance management practices and recognise organisations that demonstrate exceptional results in leadership, strategy, customer engagement, workforce development, and operational performance.\n\nTo qualify for this prestigious recognition, nominees must first be recipients of their respective National Quality Awards, a distinction CBL Foods International earned by winning the Sri Lanka National Quality Award 2023 in the Large-Scale Manufacturing category."
  },
