    "chunk_text": "Browns\u2019 General Trading honoured at Construct Exhibition 2025\n\nBrowns General Trading was proud to have been recognised as the \u2018Best Displayed Stall,\u2019 under the Hardware & Tools category at the renowned Construct Exhibition 2025, held recently at the BMICH. Organised by the National Construction Association of Sri Lanka (NCASL) for the 22nd consecutive year, the event is one of the most prestigious and anticipated conventions in the building and construction industry\u2019s annual calendar.\n\nHeld this year under the theme, \u2018Together We Can Build,\u2019 the platform brought together leaders, builders, designers and other key industry stakeholders to showcase the latest innovations that are shaping and leading the sector.\n\nWith its sleek, state-of-the-art Makita power tools, Tailin cutting wheels, Eclipse hand tools, JK files, a range of pressure washers, vacuum cleaners and generators, Juba inverter welding machines and agricultural tools under the Lion brand, Browns General Trading made a lasting impression at Construct 2025. The vibrant and interactive stall encompassed live demonstrations throughout all three days, captivating all who visited the space.\n\nCommenting on the accolade, Ajith De Silva, Cluster Chief Operating Officer, Automotive & Hardware \u2013 Brown & Company PLC said, \u201cWe are honoured to receive this recognition at Construct 2025. It reflects the dedication and passion of our team, as well as our ongoing commitment to delivering world-class tools and solutions that build and sustain Sri Lanka, while transforming its ever-changing construction landscape.\u201d"
