    "chunk_size_bytes": 1603,
    "chunk_text": "Beauty \u2026 with Ice Cubes\n\nThis week I\u2019ve decided to give The Island readers a few simple homemade beauty tips with ice cubes and water.\n\nOf course, you can add ingredients like cucumber, green tea, or rose water, to frozen ice cubes, for added benefits, like reduced puffiness, pore tightening, and a brighter complexion.\n\nRemember to always cleanse your face before applying ice and wrap the ice in a thin cloth (for sensitive skin), and avoid using ice daily, to prevent skin irritation.\n\nDip your face into the bowl, with eyes closed, for 10-15 seconds, repeating this 04-05 times.\n\nRub an ice cube gently over your face to reduce puffiness and tighten pores.\n\nIce cubes can help calm irritated skin, reducing redness and inflammation.\n\nIce cube massage can help improve circulation and tone your skin.\n\nCold temperatures cause pores to shrink, giving your skin a smoother appearance.\n\nFor pore tightening and a smoother base, before makeup, mix 04 tablespoons of cucumber juice and 02 tablespoons of rose water. Pour into an ice tray, and freeze. Then gently rub a cube over your clean face for 30 seconds.\n\nTo calm, moisturise, and brighten skin, mix concentrated rosewater with regular water, freeze, and then gently massage a cube over your face for a clean-up effect.\n\nTo control oil and reduce acne, freeze a mixture of tomato juice and a few drops of tea tree oil. Rub on oily areas of clean skin.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
