    "md5": "bc7a0cf0175c6d5b747fac89ccef740e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1599,
    "chunk_text": "Curtin University Colombo welcomes Professor Jeff Brooks\n\nProfessor Jeff S. Brooks, Head of the School of Education at Curtin University, Australia, recognised as one the world\u2019s leading voices in educational leadership and social justice, visited Colombo sharing a message of collaboration, courage, and change. His discussions with Sri Lankan educators opened new pathways for academic partnership and leadership innovation, reasserting Curtin University\u2019s commitment to global impact through education.\n\nHis visit to Sri Lanka provided a platform for knowledge exchange, emphasising the importance of global partnerships to address shared educational challenges.\n\nDuring his time in Sri Lanka, Professor Jeff Brooks engaged with a wide range of institutions and stakeholders, highlighting the importance of collaboration in advancing education. At Curtin University Colombo, he met with the leadership team and held in\u2011depth discussions with faculty and staff. These exchanges focused on strengthening academic development and exploring new avenues for institutional partnerships, strengthening the role of Curtin Colombo as a bridge between Sri Lanka and Curtin University in Perth.\n\nNDB Bank partners with Browns EV to drive the future of electric vehicles in Sri Lanka\n\nSri Lanka Insurance Life partners with Bar Association of Sri Lanka to offer exclusive retirement plans for legal fraternity\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
