    "md5": "c2bd1e61740ae7a949944d8fd0982dd3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1435,
    "chunk_text": "The timing is favourable and presents a unique opportunity. The Government\u2019s national digital agenda, including digital transformation initiatives such as the Sri Lanka Unique Digital Identity (SL-UDI) and the Digital Economic Authority (DEA), provides the infrastructure to embed crypto oversight into broader digital governance. With India, Pakistan, Thailand, and Vietnam all advancing crypto regulation, Sri Lanka cannot afford to sit idle.\n\nAmend existing laws to cover virtual assets, ensuring coherence across financial governance.\n\nDefine institutional roles: The DEA or CBSL should lead oversight, with the FIU handling AML/CFT enforcement and the SEC supervising exchanges. Introduce a taxation regime for exchanges and capital gains.\n\nEstablish regulatory sandboxes in Port City to test new services under supervision.\n\nAdvance exploration of a Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC) to strengthen financial stability, reduce dependency on cash and lower money printing costs.\n\nAlign crypto measures with Sri Lanka\u2019s 2025 digital transformation initiatives by establishing the DEA as the dedicated crypto regulatory authority, with powers to licence, register and supervise crypto service providers or VASPS and utilising Sri Lanka\u2019s SL-UDI project for KYC, AML/CFT and tax compliance.\n\nImplement public awareness campaigns tailored to different demographics, improving digital literacy and building consumer confidence."
  },
